review_text:
Very interesting story, there's some contrivances that are hard to grasp, but overall pretty intriguing.
Regarding gameplay...the game is quite easy even on suicide difficulty(M&K); 
FUBAR gets things going.... the wrong way tho, since the base cover mechanic is quite old and cluncky, the enemy's aimbot tends to be on the annoying side more than actually mechanically challenging

One of the greatest ANTI-WAR games! 

Played during December 2023 probably on a high-end PC 

Good stuff: 
One of the best video game stories: It's analogous to one of the greatest anti-war films, Apocalypse Now, but not in the way as you'd expect (multiple endings too)!
Great characters: You, the villain, etc; 
Great setting: Dubai, which is known for its opulence, has pretty much gone to ♥♥♥♥ here, and that works well, just shows America always has to save the day regardless of whether its Irag or Dubai; 
Good dialogues, interesting score, great presentation (lots of stuff change as you play through, if you can catch them); 

Good visuals (for it's time), nice sound effects, interactive game-world (for it's time);

Not so good stuff:
Game-play is clunky (it's arguably the greatest demerit of this game), 
Repetitive, 
Squad AI could have been better.

All in all, it's one of the greatest stories ever told on a video game! (It's no longer available on the Steam store, perhaps a remaster would do it justice)

